            written in the language of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            and parameters
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_1,\dots,a_n\in M
            (of appropriate
            = succeed "s)," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo ⊨
                  %mi φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi N
                  %mo ⊨
                  %mi φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \vDash \varphi(a_1,\dots,a_n) \;\iff\; N \vDash \varphi(f(a_1),\dots, f(a_n)).
          %p
            In particular, this implies that if either
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model"} model
            of some first-order
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory"} theory
          %p
            Note that the condition that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            be injective is automatic as long as the logic in question includes equality, since reflecting of the formula
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
