          %h2#elementary_embeddings_between_models_of_set_theory Elementary embeddings between models of set theory
          %h3#in_material_set_theory In material set theory
          %p
            Elementary embeddings play an important role in the study of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+cardinals"} large cardinals
            in (material)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
          %p
            For instance, the existence of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+cardinal"} measurable cardinal
            is equivalent to the existence of a non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjective
            elementary embedding
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j\colon V\to M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is the universe of sets and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+set"} transitive
            model of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZF"} ZF
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
